--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Vendored by pytran — see docs/adr/ADR-0008-*.md and vendor/README.md.

  Upstream source : CensoredUsername/unrpyc  (`legacy` line, Unrpyc v1.x)
                    MIT: Yuri K. Schlesner, CensoredUsername, Jackmcbarn
                    decompiler/codegen.py additionally under 3-clause BSD
                    (Copyright (c) 2008, Armin Ronacher) — see above.
  Upstream tag    : v1.3.2
  Vendored commit : 13f7e0ec56a7134a5afc89d70f3e48823e715f3e
  Vendored date   : 2024-08-17
  Vendored files  : unrpyc.py, deobfuscate.py, decompiler/__init__.py,
                    decompiler/{magic,astdump,atldecompiler,codegen,
                                renpycompat,screendecompiler,sl2decompiler,
                                testcasedecompiler,translate,util}.py

  Purpose: the Ren'Py 7 / 6.x fallback. Unrpyc v1 targets Ren'Py 7.x and 6.x,
  which Unrpyc v2 (vendored in vendor/unrpyc_real/) does not cover.

  IMPORTANT runtime constraint: this version requires **Python 2.7**
  (`unrpyc.py main()` raises unless `sys.version_info[:2] == (2, 7)`, and the
  sources use Python 2 syntax such as `except Exception, e:`). It therefore
  CANNOT run in the pytran interpreter (Python 3) and is only ever invoked in a
  subprocess under a Python 2.7 interpreter — typically the one bundled by the
  Ren'Py 7 game itself at `<game>/lib/windows-i686/python.exe`.

  Note: like v2, this version fakes the `renpy` package itself
  (`decompiler/renpycompat.py` -> `magic.fake_package("renpy")`), so it does
  NOT need a real Ren'Py engine — only a Python 2.7 interpreter with a working
  standard library.

Upstream sources are vendored verbatim from the v1.3.2 tag; all license texts
above are preserved unchanged. Files owned by this project (e.g. `__init__.py`
if added) carry their own headers and are not part of the vendored upstream.
